<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνίημι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>relaxed, slack,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνίαι γαστρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					6.11
				</span></i>
			; of the hair, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄ. τῆς κόμης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					1.32
				</span></i>
			:—of bodily parts, <i>relaxed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>GA</u>
				738a2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνετῶς</span> (sic <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				641
			</span></i>, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>Aphr. <i><span class="en">
				<u>in SE</u>
				121.32
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				3.1.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>set free from labour,</i> esp. of men and animals dedicated to
			a god, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				72
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					1.28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				1.110
			</span></i>; of land, <i>consecrated and lying untilled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				11.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τῶν μειρακίων ὁρμὴν ἄνετον
				εἴασαν νέμεσθαι</span>
			
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφ-</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.12a
			</span></i>; <i>uncontrolled, licentious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξουσία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					2.4.4
				</span></i>
			; <i>intemperate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμάρτημ᾽ ἄνετον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					p.60
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
